<h4 id="problems-with-captions-and-float">Problems with captions and float</h4>
<p>The <code>float:left;</code> style causes following blocks to show up on the right of
your image. So did the following paragraph in the previous example.
Inevitably, this will happen against your will. In that case, put this after
the image:</p>
<pre><code>#+begin_export html
 &#x3C;br style="clear:both;" />
#+end_export
</code></pre>
<p>Or you could use the less obtrusive syntax:</p>
<pre><code>@&#x3C;br style="clear:both;" />
</code></pre>
<h3 id="captions-in-a-row">Captions in a row</h3>
<p>In addition, <code>float:left;</code> changes the alignment of several images with caption
in a row. They now fill a row on the display, until the screen width is
filled with images. They now behave like simple text.</p>
<pre><code class="language-org">#+CAPTION: Michael
#+ATTR_HTML::alt image
[[../images/orgmode/org-mode-unicorn.png]]
#+CAPTION: Steve
#+ATTR_HTML::alt image
[[../images/orgmode/org-mode-unicorn.png]]
#+CAPTION: Carla
#+ATTR_HTML::alt image
[[../images/orgmode/org-mode-unicorn.png]]
#+CAPTION: Pete
#+ATTR_HTML::alt image
[[../images/orgmode/org-mode-unicorn.png]]

... etc. - many more ...
</code></pre>
<p>results in:</p>
<div class="minipage">
<p></p>
    <div class="figure" style="float:left;">
    <p><img src="/worg/images/orgmode/org-mode-unicorn.png" alt="image" /></p>
    <p>Michael</p>
    </div>

    <div class="figure" style="float:left;">
    <p><img src="/worg/images/orgmode/org-mode-unicorn.png" alt="image" /></p>
    <p>Steve</p>
    </div>

    <div class="figure" style="float:left;">
    <p><img src="/worg/images/orgmode/org-mode-unicorn.png" alt="image" /></p>
    <p>Carla</p>
    </div>

    <div class="figure" style="float:left;">
    <p><img src="/worg/images/orgmode/org-mode-unicorn.png" alt="image" /></p>
    <p>Pete</p>
    </div>

